  "instance_name": "cultural_justification_of_violence",
  "label": "Cultural Justification of Violence",
  "description": "The idea that certain acts of violence or repression are deemed acceptable or necessary within a specific cultural or social context. This concept is central to understanding the first panel’s claim that 'honor killings are part of our culture.' The meme critiques this notion by juxtaposing it with a violent, militaristic response, highlighting the absurdity and moral bankruptcy of using culture to justify murder.",
